  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The patch on the seventh of August implemented a huge FBT change that made the avatars head follow your HMD 100% of the time, stretching/withdrawing either your Chest or Neck to accomodate the movement.\n\"Your avatar will be attached or \"pinned\" to your HMD. This allows your viewpoint to always be correct, assuming you've set it correctly in the SDK.\"\nHowever in the recent week or 2 Ive realized that that isnt the case anymore and my Avatar reacts just like it did before the August update, with my hmd being inside the neck or top of the chest.\nAs a side note I did upgrade from Hybrid Rift CV1 with Vive Trackers to Index with Vive Trackers.\nDoubt this plays a role but who knows.",
